  "investigation_notes": "Current status: `incidentlab-app-1` is running (E1,E4) but unhealthy - `/health` returns 503 `unhealthy` (E2).\n\nRoot cause is dependency outage, not storage:\n\n* `incidentlab-db-1` is `exited` (E1) with `exit_code 0`, `running false` (E5), `finished_at 2026-10-28T16:52:20.590421414Z` (E5).\n* DB log shows graceful shutdown: `received fast shutdown request` / `database system is shut down` (E6), no crash/corruption, `oom_killed false` (E5).\n* Events show `kill` + `stop` + `die exit_code 0` at `16:52:20` (E8) after successful `pg_isready exit 0` checks (E8). This rules in intentional stop vs crash.\n* App `health` failure at `16:52:23` is `psycopg.OperationalError: failed to resolve host 'db': Temporary failure in name resolution` in `main.py line 98 health psycopg.connect` (E3).\n* Both containers were on `incidentlab_default` (E4,E5), so `db` DNS failure is expected consequence of db being stopped, not separate network issue.\n* App itself did not restart (`restart_count 0`), not OOM (`oom_killed false`) (E4).\n\nStorage / uploads path currently ruled OUT as cause:\n\n* Historical symptom in app log: `File /app/main.py line 58 upload out.write(chunk) OSError [Errno 28] No space left on device` (E3).\n* That is not current state: `/srv/lab-data` has `use_percent 7.8%`, `available 416.2 MB`, `inode 0.1%` (E7). Root `/` has `use 6.4%`, `inode 1.4%` (E11).\n* `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is `owner 1000:1000 mode 0755` with `app_uid 1000 app_user_can_write true` (E9). Parent `/srv/lab-data` same (E10). App runs as `1000:1000` (E4) with bind `source /srv/lab-data destination /data rw true` (E4).\n* Same app log shows successful `POST /upload 200 OK` and `GET /files 200 OK` after the `Errno 28` line at `16:46:12` and again at `16:52:20` (E3), proving writes succeeded later.\n\nConclusion:\n\nUpload outage symptom coincides with unhealthy app due to stopped DB dependency. File-system full and permission-denied are ruled out by current space (E7,E11) and writability (E9,E10). Prior `No space left` (E3) was transient/historical.\n",
